            "purpose": "Produce independent evidence on two changed simple series circuits and expose exactly which sub-skill, if any, needs remediation.",
            "instructions": "Solve these two changed simple series circuits without help. Q1: A series circuit has a 12 V source and two resistors, R1 = 3 ohm and R2 = 6 ohm. Find the total resistance, the current through the circuit, and the voltage across each resistor. Q2: A series circuit has a 9 V source and three resistors, R1 = 2 ohm, R2 = 3 ohm and R3 = 4 ohm. Find the total resistance, the current, and the voltage across each resistor. For each question, state the series rules you used (same current through all components, resistances add, source voltage divides across resistors in proportion to resistance) and show the substitution into each formula. Check each answer by verifying that the resistor voltages add to the source voltage. Record any step where you were unsure and explain what rule you should have applied there.",
